+## Evidence
+
+**What this PR solves.** Persistent agents act only when something prompts
+them, and what survives compaction is whatever the summarizer kept. This PR
+lets a session elect its own next turn (`continue_work`), send work to
+background sub-agents whose results return to it (`continue_delegate`), and ask
+for compaction once it has saved its state (`request_compaction`). It is
+designed so that accepted work survives restart, compaction and session
+rollover. The checks below cover regressions at this exact head; its live
+behavior proofs are still pending (see the end of this section).
+
+**Head checked:** `16541aa5a8ee81f1e505a414e2d21a758c43cbc2`, which carries
+upstream `main` at `1129d4c0716c7dcc6fba86753ec214584ec8ebd1`. It replaces the
+earlier presented head `9bfc4d31` by a non-fast-forward update. The 22
+continuation commits on `9bfc4d31` that this head doesn't share by SHA each
+have a patch-identical commit here (`git patch-id --stable`). The other
+commits it no longer carries are either from the fork's deployment line,
+outside this feature, or merges of older upstream `main`, which this head
+already contains. "Previous candidate" below means `93a1e356`, the gated
+candidate before this one, which this PR never presented.
+
